  "legalTitle": "Legal",
  "legalSettingsBody": "Privacy policy, Terms of Use, and data handling",
  "legalIntroTitle": "Clear, honest policies",
  "legalIntroBody": "How MassLens handles your data and the rules that apply when you use the app.",
  "legalPrivacyPolicy": "Privacy policy",
  "legalTermsOfUse": "Terms of use",
  "legalLastUpdated": "15 Aug 2026",
  "legalPublishedPolicy": "View published privacy policy",
  "legalFooter": "MassLens · Legal documents",
  "legalPrivacyScopeTitle": "Scope and who provides MassLens",
  "legalPrivacyScopeBody": "MassLens is provided by the developer identified on its Google Play listing (\"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"). This policy explains how information is handled in the MassLens Android app and its scan service. MassLens does not require an account and does not directly ask for your name, email address, profile, or precise location.",
  "legalPrivacyPhotosTitle": "Photos and AI analysis",
  "legalPrivacyPhotosBody": "A photo is processed only when you choose Camera or Gallery and start an AI scan. Before upload, MassLens corrects orientation, resizes the image, re-encodes it as JPEG, and removes embedded EXIF and GPS metadata. The photo, an optional second angle, and scan context are sent over HTTPS through the MassLens Cloudflare service to OpenAI to identify visible objects or food and estimate weight ranges. OpenAI is instructed not to store the response. Photos are not stored in the MassLens Worker database.",
  "legalPrivacyNutritionTitle": "Food scans and USDA data",
  "legalPrivacyNutritionBody": "For Food & macros scans, the AI returns food labels, approximate weight ranges, and generic English search terms; it does not create nutrient values. The server sends only normalized food search text to USDA FoodData Central to find calories and macros. USDA never receives your photos, installation identifier, or local history. All food weights, calories, and macros are estimates and may be incomplete.",
  "legalPrivacyLocalTitle": "Information stored on your device",
  "legalPrivacyLocalBody": "Scan results and a private image copy are saved only when you choose Save. Preferences, local scan history, and Nutrition & Trends entries are stored inside the app on your device. Nutrition entries are added only when you explicitly import a saved food scan or enter values manually; they are not uploaded. Bluetooth device information is used only to find and connect to compatible scales and is not sent to MassLens. Android backup behavior may depend on your device settings.",
  "legalPrivacyServiceTitle": "Service data and retention",
  "legalPrivacyServiceBody": "MassLens creates a random installation identifier to manage starter scans, rewarded scan credits, retries, and abuse prevention. The service hashes it before database use and records request identifiers, credit state, reward state, limited technical events, and anonymous daily totals such as completed scan mode and AI cost. A completed result JSON, never the photo, may be retained for up to 24 hours for idempotent retries. Credit and anti-abuse records are kept as needed to operate those features. Hosting and network providers may process IP addresses and routine security logs.",
  "legalPrivacyAdsTitle": "Advertising and consent",
  "legalPrivacyAdsBody": "MassLens uses Google Mobile Ads for rewarded scan credits and other ad placements. Google and its advertising partners may process advertising identifiers, device information, approximate location derived from network signals, diagnostics, consent choices, and ad interactions under their own policies. Where required, the app requests consent. If Google makes privacy options available for you, they can be reviewed from Settings.",
  "legalPrivacySharingTitle": "Service providers, transfers, and sale",
  "legalPrivacySharingBody": "Information is shared only as needed with Cloudflare for API delivery, OpenAI for photo analysis, USDA FoodData Central for generic nutrition searches, and Google for advertising and consent. These providers may process information in countries other than yours under their own terms and safeguards. MassLens does not sell your local scan history or nutrition diary and does not use them for user-level nutrition advertising or analytics.",
  "legalPrivacyChoicesTitle": "Your choices and deletion",
  "legalPrivacyChoicesBody": "You can deny camera or Bluetooth permission, use the simulator or compatible Bluetooth scale without AI, cancel before analysis, decline to save results, delete individual scans, clear all estimate history, clear Nutrition & Trends separately, review available ad privacy choices, or uninstall the app. Uninstalling removes app-local data subject to Android backup settings. For privacy requests that cannot be completed on-device, use the developer contact details on the MassLens Google Play listing. Do not send photos or sensitive health information with your request.",
  "legalPrivacySecurityTitle": "Security and children",
  "legalPrivacySecurityBody": "MassLens uses HTTPS, metadata removal, hashed installation identifiers, and access controls designed to reduce risk. No storage or internet transmission can be guaranteed completely secure. MassLens is not directed to children below the minimum digital-consent age in their country, and we do not knowingly request personal profiles from children.",
  "legalPrivacyChangesTitle": "Changes and contact",
  "legalPrivacyChangesBody": "This policy may change when MassLens, applicable law, or its service providers change. The last-updated date will be revised for material updates. The published HTTPS version linked above is the version intended for the Google Play listing. Questions may be sent using the developer contact shown on that listing.",
  "legalTermsAcceptanceTitle": "Acceptance and eligibility",
  "legalTermsAcceptanceBody": "By installing or using MassLens, you agree to these Terms of Use and the Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the app. You must be legally able to accept these terms where you live; otherwise, a parent or legal guardian must review and accept them for you. You are responsible for complying with applicable laws.",
  "legalTermsServiceTitle": "What the service provides",
  "legalTermsServiceBody": "MassLens provides compatible Bluetooth-scale readings, a clearly labeled touch simulator, AI-assisted visual estimates for objects and food plates, USDA-based approximate nutrition, local history, and an optional local nutrition diary. Features may require a supported device, internet access, permissions, ad availability, or a remaining scan credit.",
  "legalTermsEstimatesTitle": "Estimates, nutrition, and safety",
  "legalTermsEstimatesBody": "AI scans are visual estimates, not physical scale readings. Results may be inaccurate, incomplete, or unsuitable for a particular item or meal. MassLens is not a medical device and does not provide medical, dietary, allergy, dosing, legal-trade, shipping, or safety advice. Never rely on it for medication, regulated commerce, allergens, hazardous materials, or other safety-critical decisions. Use a calibrated scale or qualified professional when accuracy matters.",
  "legalTermsContentTitle": "Your photos and acceptable use",
  "legalTermsContentBody": "You keep your rights in photos and information you submit. You give MassLens and its necessary service providers a limited permission to process them only to deliver the requested scan, maintain security, and provide retries as described in the Privacy Policy. You must have the right to use submitted images. Do not submit illegal content, intimate imagery, confidential documents, images that violate another person's privacy or rights, malicious code, or content unrelated to legitimate object or food analysis.",
  "legalTermsCreditsTitle": "Scan credits and advertising",
  "legalTermsCreditsBody": "A new installation may receive a limited number of starter scans. A completed rewarded advertisement may grant a scan credit after confirmation by the app and service. Credits have no cash value, cannot be transferred, and may be limited to prevent abuse. Ad availability is not guaranteed. Failed qualifying scans are normally refunded, but access may be delayed by outages, fraud checks, or technical errors. Advertising formats and credit rules may change with reasonable notice.",
  "legalTermsThirdPartyTitle": "Local data and third-party services",
  "legalTermsThirdPartyBody": "Saved results and nutrition entries are stored locally and may be lost if you delete them, clear app data, uninstall, change devices, or lose the device. You are responsible for any backup you require. MassLens relies on services from Cloudflare, OpenAI, USDA FoodData Central, Google Mobile Ads, Google Play, and device manufacturers. Their services, content, and availability are governed by their own terms; MassLens does not control them.",
  "legalTermsLicenseTitle": "License and intellectual property",
  "legalTermsLicenseBody": "You receive a limited, personal, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use MassLens for lawful, non-commercial purposes. The app, design, code, branding, and original materials remain the property of their respective owners. You may not copy, sell, sublicense, reverse engineer except where law expressly permits, bypass security or credit controls, overload the service, scrape it, or use it to build a competing dataset or service.",
  "legalTermsAvailabilityTitle": "Availability, changes, and misuse",
  "legalTermsAvailabilityBody": "MassLens may change, suspend, or discontinue features to improve the app, address security or legal requirements, manage costs, or respond to third-party changes. Continuous, error-free availability is not promised. Access may be limited or blocked when reasonably necessary to prevent fraud, automated abuse, attacks, unlawful use, or harm to the service or others.",
  "legalTermsLiabilityTitle": "Disclaimers and limitation of liability",
  "legalTermsLiabilityBody": "To the fullest extent permitted by law, MassLens is provided \"as is\" and \"as available\" without warranties of accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose, uninterrupted operation, or error-free results. The developer is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary losses arising from reliance on estimates, loss of local data, third-party services, ads, or inability to use the app. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot legally be excluded in your country.",
  "legalTermsChangesTitle": "Updates, severability, and contact",
  "legalTermsChangesBody": "These terms may be updated when MassLens or applicable requirements change. Continuing to use the app after an update takes effect means you accept the revised terms where permitted by law. If one provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to apply. Applicable mandatory consumer law remains unaffected. For questions or legal notices, use the developer contact details on the MassLens Google Play listing.",
